-- title:
--   Spreading out étaleness of a level ring over ℤ[1/f]
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \neq p$. Write $A$ for `Afin p`, the finite-$j$ chart subalgebra `chartAlgFin` of the full modular function field of level $p$ over $\mathbf{Z}$ attached to the modular function `jFull p`, and for an integer $f$ write $A[1/f]$ for the localization of $A$ away from the image of $f$. Given $u \in A$ and $g \in \mathbf{Z}[X]$, the level ring `levelRing p f u g` is the quotient $A[1/f]/(g(u))$, where $g$ is evaluated at the image of $u$ in $A[1/f]$. Assume that $B := A[1/p]/(g(u))$ is a finite and flat module over $\mathbf{Z}[1/p] =$ `Localization.Away (p : ℤ)`, that for every prime ideal $P$ of $\mathbf{Z}[1/p]$ with $P = \bot$ the fibre $P$`.Fiber` $B$ is étale over the residue field of $P$, and that the same holds for every prime ideal $P$ equal to the ideal generated by the image of $\ell$. Then there exists an integer $c$ with $c \neq 0$, $\ell \nmid c$ and $p \mid c$ such that for every nonzero integer $f$ divisible by $c$ the level ring $A[1/f]/(g(u))$ is étale over $\mathbf{Z}[1/f]$.
--
--   This is the spreading-out step for the level rings of the integral two-chart model: étaleness of the generic fibre and of the fibre at $\ell$ over $\mathbf{Z}[1/p]$ is propagated to étaleness over $\mathbf{Z}[1/f]$ for all $f$ in a suitable divisibility class, chosen so that $p$ divides and $\ell$ does not divide the controlling integer $c$. It rests on the general criterion [`Algebra.exists_etale_localizationAway_of_forall_isEtaleAt`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_etale_localizationAway_of_forall_isEtaleAt) and is used by [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_HpoolLevelRing_exists_forall_etale_levelRing_of_etale_fiber.lean

